---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="MIAR Website Terms"
  description="Terms for use of the public MIAR website and request-access form."
  current="terms"
>
  <main class="subpage-shell legal-document-shell">
    <header class="legal-document-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Website terms</p>
      <h1>Terms for using the public MIAR site.</h1>
      <div class="legal-document-meta">
        <span>Effective 30 July 2026</span>
        <span>Public website and request-access form</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="legal-document">
      <aside>
        <p>These are website terms, not product or imagery licence terms.</p>
        <a href="/privacy/">Privacy notice</a>
        <a href="/legal/">Legal overview</a>
      </aside>

      <div class="legal-document-body">
        <section>
          <h2>Purpose of the site</h2>
          <p>
            This site provides public information about MIAR and a form for organizations to
            request contact or access review. It is not an open self-service platform.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>No access right is created</h2>
          <p>
            Submitting a form does not create an account, contract, evaluation licence,
            procurement commitment, or right to receive a response. ReachDefence may accept,
            defer, or refuse a request.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Permitted use</h2>
          <p>
            You may use the public site for lawful informational and organizational evaluation
            purposes. You must not interfere with the site, attempt unauthorized access, submit
            false identity or organization information, automate abusive requests, or use the
            site in breach of applicable law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Sensitive information</h2>
          <p>
            Do not submit classified, export-controlled, operationally sensitive, personal
            data about third parties, or other restricted information through the public form.
            A use-case description should remain at an unclassified, non-sensitive level.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Eligibility and jurisdiction</h2>
          <p>
            MIAR is not offered in every jurisdiction. Access may be blocked, refused, or
            withdrawn based on location, identity, intended use, sanctions, export controls,
            compliance obligations, or security risk. The current public form does not accept
            requests identified as originating from China or Pakistan.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Site content</h2>
          <p>
            Site content describes current positioning and intended capabilities at a general
            level. It is not a warranty, service-level commitment, technical specification, or
            promise that a feature, data source, deployment pattern, or delivery time is
            available to a particular customer.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
          <p>
            The site design, copy, graphics, MIAR name, and ReachDefence branding may be
            protected by intellectual-property law. No licence is granted except the limited
            right to view the public site for its intended purpose. Third-party imagery,
            basemaps, marks, and data remain subject to their respective rights and licences.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>External links</h2>
          <p>
            Links to third-party sites are provided for reference. ReachDefence does not control
            their availability, content, security, or privacy practices.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
          <p>
            The public site may be changed, restricted, or withdrawn without notice. Separate
            written terms will govern any pilot, demonstration, data-sharing arrangement,
            imagery licence, API access, or production deployment.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
